#
# precompiled.list - the shader sources compiled ahead of time, for every table.
#
# One list, read by every table generator, so that what the tables hold is
# decided in one place:
#
#   tools/glsl2usc.sh              the PowerVR table from Mesa's pco_shc
#                                  (tests/reference/blobs.rs): the `src`, `blend`,
#                                  `for` and `skip-failures` lines;
#   tools/vivante/gen_shader_table.py
#                                  the GC7000 table from Mesa's etna_shc
#                                  (tests/reference/vivante_blobs.rs): the `dir`
#                                  lines (its directory allowlist);
#   yakogl-precompile              the table our own compiler builds at image
#                                  build time (tools/precompile; into build/,
#                                  never committed): all of it, `pair` included;
#                                  with --internal, the back ends' own programs
#                                  (committed): the `internal` lines.
#
# Paths are relative to tools/shaders/. A line is whitespace-separated fields;
# `#` starts a comment, on a line of its own or after the fields.
#
#   dir DIR ROLE...       DIR (`.` is tools/shaders itself) holds shaders, and
#                         is for ROLE: `gc7000`, the GC7000 table takes every
#                         shader in it; `internal`, the back ends' own shaders,
#                         which no table holds (the `internal` lines name the
#                         ones our compiler builds the back ends' programs from);
#                         `-`, neither. Every directory under tools/shaders/
#                         that holds a .vert or .frag must have a line, and a
#                         `src` or `pair` path must lie in a listed directory:
#                         a directory nobody was told about fails every reader
#                         (gen_shader_table.py's TABLE_DIRS guard; its wedge
#                         probes are why).
#   src PATH              an input of the PowerVR table, in table order (the
#                         order is the table's row order). PATH may end in a
#                         glob (`*`, `?`) over one directory's files, which
#                         expands in byte order; an empty expansion is nothing.
#   blend SPEC            a variant every fragment shader is compiled for as
#                         well as its plain form, unless a `for` line matches
#                         it. SPEC is glsl2usc's --blend syntax:
#                         FACTORS[:MASK][@RT], FACTORS `srgb,drgb[,sa,da[,eq[,eqa]]]`
#                         (Mesa's factor names: one, zero, src_alpha,
#                         inv_src_alpha, ...; equations add, sub, rsub, min,
#                         max) or `replace`, MASK the colour channels written
#                         (r g b a), RT the render target class (rgba8, f16x4,
#                         f16, f32).
#   for GLOB SPEC[;SPEC]  the variants of the fragment shaders whose path
#                         matches GLOB (`*` also crosses `/`), INSTEAD of the
#                         `blend` lines; the first matching `for` wins.
#   skip-failures         pco_shc: a source it cannot build is reported and left
#                         out of the table instead of failing the run.
#   app NAME              the `pair` lines after it are one application's.
#   internal GPU NAME SOURCE [SPEC]
#                         a program a back end binds itself, not an
#                         application's: GPU `powervr` or `gc7000`, NAME the
#                         program's name in that back end's table, SOURCE a
#                         .vert or .frag of an `internal` directory -- or, on
#                         the PowerVR, `attach:N`, the clear-attach program of
#                         N dwords our encoder builds (it moves packed colour
#                         words, which no GLSL says) -- and SPEC, for a
#                         fragment shader, the variant the back end binds (the
#                         `blend` syntax). `yakogl-precompile --internal`
#                         compiles a GPU's lines with our compiler into its
#                         committed table, src/pvr/internal.rs or
#                         src/vivante/internal.rs, in list order; the other
#                         generators read none of them.
#   pair VS FS            a program the application links. Our generator links
#                         it as glLinkProgram does, so the records a link makes
#                         (a fragment shader recompiled with a varying the
#                         vertex shader never writes read as 0, or for a
#                         constant gl_Position.w; a vertex shader laid out with
#                         the program's attribute locations) are compiled
#                         ahead of time too, and the variants are asked for of
#                         the linked fragment shader, as a draw asks.
#
# The GPUs. The GC7000 has no blend variants (blending and colour masks are
# pixel-engine state there), so `blend` and `for` are PowerVR-only; its one
# variant, the opposite front-face winding of a shader that reads
# gl_FrontFacing, is implied rather than listed. The PowerVR table holds the
# `src` lines; the GC7000 table every shader of a `gc7000` directory, which
# leaves out `offarm/` (the PowerVR measurement series of gl_test 193 and 194; the
# GC7000 runs 193 in an online image only) and `internal/`.
#
# Our compiler's sources: the PowerVR build takes the `src` lines and every
# source a `pair` names; the GC7000 build every shader of a `gc7000`
# directory and the pair sources in them. A source our compiler refuses
# (tests/fixtures/online_refused_<gpu>[_es2].txt, which tests/online_corpus.rs
# pins message for message) is reported and left out, with every pair that
# names it; any other failure fails the run. The internal directories hold
# no table's sources: `internal/` is GLSL 450 for Mesa (the reference
# programs in tests/reference/, tools/glsl2usc.sh's usc-blob calls and
# gen_shader_table.py's clear_shader), `internal/es/` the GLSL ES twins our
# compiler builds the back ends' programs from (the `internal` lines below).

dir .              gc7000
dir es100          gc7000
dir es300          gc7000
dir femtovg        gc7000
dir gl_test_es100  gc7000
dir qt             gc7000
dir qt3d           gc7000
dir offarm         -          # PowerVR-only: gl_test 193/194's predicated-off arm, grown by N
dir gl_test_own    -          # gl_test's own sources (cases 181-183, 188-192; its README): in no Mesa table, linked by the `pair` lines below
dir internal       internal   # fbload.*, clear.*: Mesa's reference programs (tools/glsl2usc.sh, gen_shader_table.py)
dir internal/es    internal   # their GLSL ES twins: the `internal` lines

# ---- the back ends' own programs (yakogl-precompile --internal) -------------
# The PowerVR's: the quad every frame and clear quad draws with; the frame
# load (a frame that does not clear its target copies what is there), one per
# render-target class; the masked clears (glColorMask lowered into the shader:
# M, bit 0 R .. 3 A, the channels written), RGBA8 and RGBA16F; the
# background object's clear-attach programs for 1, 2 and 3 dwords.

internal powervr quad_vs        internal/es/quad.vert
internal powervr fbload         internal/es/fbload.frag
internal powervr fbload_f16x4   internal/es/fbload.frag replace@f16x4
internal powervr fbload_f16     internal/es/fbload.frag replace@f16
internal powervr fbload_f32     internal/es/fbload.frag replace@f32
internal powervr clear_m1       internal/es/clear.frag replace:r
internal powervr clear_m1_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:r@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m2       internal/es/clear.frag replace:g
internal powervr clear_m2_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:g@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m3       internal/es/clear.frag replace:rg
internal powervr clear_m3_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:rg@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m4       internal/es/clear.frag replace:b
internal powervr clear_m4_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:b@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m5       internal/es/clear.frag replace:rb
internal powervr clear_m5_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:rb@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m6       internal/es/clear.frag replace:gb
internal powervr clear_m6_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:gb@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m7       internal/es/clear.frag replace:rgb
internal powervr clear_m7_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:rgb@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m8       internal/es/clear.frag replace:a
internal powervr clear_m8_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:a@f16x4
internal powervr clear_m9       internal/es/clear.frag replace:ra
internal powervr clear_m9_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:ra@f16x4
internal powervr clear_ma       internal/es/clear.frag replace:ga
internal powervr clear_ma_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:ga@f16x4
internal powervr clear_mb       internal/es/clear.frag replace:rga
internal powervr clear_mb_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:rga@f16x4
internal powervr clear_mc       internal/es/clear.frag replace:ba
internal powervr clear_mc_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:ba@f16x4
internal powervr clear_md       internal/es/clear.frag replace:rba
internal powervr clear_md_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:rba@f16x4
internal powervr clear_me       internal/es/clear.frag replace:gba
internal powervr clear_me_f16x4 internal/es/clear.frag replace:gba@f16x4
internal powervr clear_attach1  attach:1
internal powervr clear_attach2  attach:2
internal powervr clear_attach3  attach:3

# The GC7000's: its clear quad (blending and colour masks are pixel-engine
# state there, so one fragment shader clears every mask).

internal gc7000  clear_vs       internal/es/quad.vert
internal gc7000  clear_ps       internal/es/clear.frag

# ---- the PowerVR table's inputs (tools/glsl2usc.sh), in its row order -------

src uniform_color.frag
src passthrough.vert
src interp_color.frag
src color_uv.vert
src color_uv.frag
src mvp.vert
src texture.frag
src uv.vert
src texture2.frag
src compact.frag
src points.vert
src mvp_color.vert
src zorder.vert
src es100/matattr2.vert
src es100/matattr3.vert
src es100/matattr4.vert
src es100/matattr.frag
src es100/hello.vert
src es100/hello.frag
src es100/textured.vert
src es100/textured.frag
src es300/cube.vert
src es300/cube.frag
src es300/array.frag
src es300/vid.vert
src es300/vcolor.frag
src es300/hdrsample.frag
src es300/dynidx.frag
src es300/texsize.frag
src es300/inst.vert
src es300/inst2.vert
src es300/vol.frag
src es300/facing.frag
# FemtoVG 0.26 (Slint's GPU renderer): 1 VS + 15 FS (+14 NO_DISCARD),
# reproduced byte-exactly by `yakogl-tools femtovg-shaders`. All are GLSL ES
# 1.00 with EDGE_AA on.
src femtovg/main.vert
src femtovg/fill_color.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient.frag
src femtovg/stencil.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient.frag
src femtovg/filter_image.frag
src femtovg/texture_copy_unclipped.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.frag
src femtovg/fill_image.frag
src femtovg/fill_color.glyph.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient.glyph.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient.glyph.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.glyph.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.glyph.frag
src femtovg/fill_image.glyph.frag
# The same fragment shaders without the stroke-threshold discard (NO_DISCARD):
# the no_std fork picks them for every draw whose threshold is negative (all
# fills), which keeps those draws off the punch-through path.
src femtovg/fill_color.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/stencil.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/filter_image.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_image.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_color.glyph.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient.glyph.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient.glyph.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.glyph.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.glyph.nodiscard.frag
src femtovg/fill_image.glyph.nodiscard.frag
# gl_test cases 28..33: the bisection of the FemtoVG "invisible fill" (main.vert
# with a tiny diagnostic FS each), kept as regression tests
src fvgtest_green.frag
src fvgtest_ftcoord.frag
src fvgtest_inner.frag
src fvgtest_cover.frag
src fvgtest_discard.frag
src fvgtest_discard2.frag
src es300/cubelodv.vert
src es300/cubelodv.frag
src es300/cubelodf.vert
src es300/cubelodf.frag
# gl_test 193 offarm: fill_color.nodiscard with 8, 32 and 128 dependent
# steps in the scissor arm a zero radius never runs (N = 0 is the femtovg
# row above). The table image times them against the online compile.
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm8.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm32.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm128.frag
# gl_test 194 offarmn: the finer series (tools/gen_offarm.py writes them all)
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm2.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm4.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm12.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm16.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm24.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm48.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm64.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm96.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm192.frag
src offarm/fill_color.nodiscard.offarm256.frag
# Qt Quick's scene-graph shaders (qt6-for-zephyr: the GLSL ES 1.00 text Qt's
# GLES2 RHI backend hands to glShaderSource, extracted from the Stage 1 .qsb
# files by zephyr-module/tools/qsb2glsl; shaders/qt/README.md).
src qt/*.vert
src qt/*.frag
# Qt Quick 3D (shaders/qt3d/README.md): the runtime renderer's built-in
# shaders from the Stage 1 .qsb files plus the application's materials from
# shadergen's .qsbc collection. The ES 3.0-only built-ins have no GLSL 100
# text and never reach this list.
src qt3d/*.vert
src qt3d/*.frag

# ---- blend / colour-mask / render-target variants (PowerVR) -----------------

# Blend / colour-mask variants precompiled for every fragment shader (both
# are lowered into the FS on this GPU): GL's usual SRC_ALPHA/ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA
# (also with alpha masked off), premultiplied ONE/ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA, additive
# ONE/ONE, CONSTANT_COLOR/ONE_MINUS_CONSTANT_COLOR (reads glBlendColor) and a
# plain write of the green and alpha channels only.
blend src_alpha,inv_src_alpha
blend src_alpha,inv_src_alpha:rgb
blend one,inv_src_alpha
blend one,one
blend const_color,inv_const_color
blend replace:ga
# Colour mask with every channel off for shaders that `discard`: the GL core
# cannot disable the ISP tag writes for those (the punch-through pass then
# never updates depth/stencil, gl_test case 38), so it runs the shader with
# this variant, which writes the destination back unchanged.
blend zero,one
# FemtoVG composite operations (lib.rs CompositeOperationState; src==dst for
# both channels). SourceOver (one,inv_src_alpha), Lighter (one,one) and Copy
# (= the base shader) are already covered above.
blend dst_alpha,zero
blend inv_dst_alpha,zero
blend dst_alpha,inv_src_alpha
blend inv_dst_alpha,one
blend zero,src_alpha
blend zero,inv_src_alpha
blend inv_dst_alpha,src_alpha
blend inv_dst_alpha,inv_src_alpha
blend src_alpha,one

# Qt's scene graph blends with ONE/ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA only (premultiplied
# materials; opaque ones do not blend; stencil clips mask every channel,
# which needs no variant), so the Qt fragment shaders get just that state
# instead of the FemtoVG list.
for qt/*            one,inv_src_alpha
# Qt Quick 3D: opaque geometry does not blend; transparent materials blend
# premultiplied like the scene graph. Float render targets (Quick 3D's
# prefiltered probes are RGBA16F, its shadow maps R16F/R32F): the colour
# output packed for each class. one,inv_src_alpha@f16x4: Quick 3D's
# SourceOver (premultiplied) blended into the RGBA16F target a layer with
# post-processing renders to (qquick3dscenerenderer.cpp, postProcessingNeeded
# = firstEffect). The .frag rule must precede the catch-all (first match
# wins).
for qt3d/*.frag     one,inv_src_alpha;replace@f16x4;replace@f16;replace@f32;one,inv_src_alpha@f16x4
for qt3d/*          one,inv_src_alpha
# The ES 3.00 test shaders get the Quick 3D float-target classes too. In
# glsl2usc.sh this rule and the two above were added only when qt3d/ held a
# fragment shader; qt3d/ is committed, so here they always apply.
for es300/*.frag    one,inv_src_alpha;replace@f16x4;replace@f16;replace@f32;one,inv_src_alpha@f16x4

# A source pco_shc cannot build (so far Quick 3D's particle shaders, which are
# not GLSL ES 1.00; shaders/known-uncompilable.txt) is left out rather than
# failing the whole table.
skip-failures

# ---- the programs the applications link ------------------------------------
#
# Our generator links these. A fragment shader that no pair names gets its
# variants from its plain record, which is what a link that substitutes
# nothing hands the draw.
#
# Not knowable from this repository, so not listed:
#   - Qt Quick and Qt Quick 3D: Qt's RHI forms its programs at run time from
#     its material system. shaders/qt/README.md names a file convention
#     (<name>.vert or <name>.batchable.vert with <name>.frag), but nothing here
#     records which programs Qt actually links, and the harvested qt3d/<sha>.*
#     sources have no partner named at all.
#   - gl_test's case_psizvpm links two vertex shaders written inline in
#     gl_test.c (psizvpm_plain_vs_src, psizvpm_word_vs_src), and gl_test's
#     other inline sources likewise (184 depchain and 185 kindcost among
#     them): they are not files a list can name. The sources of 181 to 183
#     and 188 to 192 were such literals until they moved to gl_test_own/
#     (read by gen_gl_test_shaders.py like every other file), which is why
#     those cases are listed.
#   - glBindAttribLocation: a pair is linked with no bindings, so attributes
#     take the lowest free locations in declaration order, as an application
#     that binds none gets them.

# Slint (driver/samples/zephyr/slint) and the cluster (driver/samples/zephyr/
# cluster) draw through Slint's FemtoVG renderer, whose no_std fork
# (slint/nostd/femtovg-0.26.0-nostd.patch, MainProgram::new) links main.vert
# with every fragment shader of femtovg/ at start-up: the nine shader types,
# the six that take the glyph texture, both again without the stroke-threshold
# discard (texture_copy_unclipped has none to drop), and the six fills without
# the scissor mask (.nodiscard.noscissor; optional, a failed one keeps the
# masked program).
app femtovg
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_color.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_color.glyph.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_color.glyph.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_color.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_color.nodiscard.noscissor.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient.glyph.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient.glyph.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient.nodiscard.noscissor.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.glyph.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.glyph.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_gradient_conic.nodiscard.noscissor.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image.glyph.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image.glyph.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image.nodiscard.noscissor.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient.glyph.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient.glyph.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient.nodiscard.noscissor.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.glyph.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.glyph.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/fill_image_gradient_conic.nodiscard.noscissor.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/filter_image.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/filter_image.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/stencil.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/stencil.nodiscard.frag
pair femtovg/main.vert femtovg/texture_copy_unclipped.frag

# gl_test (driver/tools/pvrlab/gl_test.c): every program it links, read out
